B.auy=new A.vH("BridgePoint welcomes you by profile name and summarizes new evidence, refreshed sources, opportunity changes, alerts, and follow-ups from the last 24 hours.",B.nr,"Start with your Daily Brief")
B.aut=new A.vH("Map colors identify the opportunity: amber for roofing, red for fire, purple for storms, blue for flood/FEMA, green for solar or investment, and cyan for commercial or development.",B.ta,"See different opportunities instantly")
B.aux=new A.vH("Opportunity score ranks potential. Confidence measures evidence reliability. \u201cWhy this property,\u201d \u201cWhy now,\u201d evidence counts, and a suggested next action explain every lead.",B.kW,"Understand why\u2014without jargon")
B.auv=new A.vH("Save an opportunity, choose a lead stage, add a preset or custom note, and schedule the next action. My Work keeps the pipeline and calendar together.",B.A4,"Turn intelligence into work")
B.aus=new A.vH("Choose which alerts you want. BridgePoint refreshes in the background and keeps your Daily Brief and notification history synchronized across devices.",B.kG,"Stay ahead automatically")
B.ah2=s([B.auy,B.aut,B.aux,B.auv,B.aus],A.aK("L<+body,icon,title(l,I,l)>"))
B.Cv=s([B.U,B.BG,B.bp,B.bb,B.cP,B.dI,B.BL,B.j6,B.BM,B.BN,B.BH,B.BI,B.BJ,B.BK],A.aK("L<iK>"))
B.atB=new A.fX("The score ranks how actionable a property looks after BridgePoint checks evidence strength, recency, confidence, source diversity, property fit, and the model\u2019s strict gates. It is a prioritization tool\u2014not a guarantee of a sale, loss, permit, or claim.","What does an opportunity score mean?")
B.atQ=new A.fX("Score estimates opportunity priority. Confidence estimates how reliable and well-supported the evidence is. A high score with weak confidence should not clear the strict ranking gate.","What is confidence, and how is it different from score?")
B.atX=new A.fX("A signal is one supporting observation. A pattern connects multiple observations over time. A model match is direct evidence that satisfies a specific opportunity rule. Patterns can add context, but a property with no qualifying direct match should not outrank corroborated opportunities in strict mode.","Why do matches, signals, and patterns show different counts?")
B.aui=new A.fX("Yes. BridgePoint scoring can subtract points when direct matches or corroboration are missing, evidence is older, source diversity is weak, or confidence is lower. The intelligence suite also keeps only the best qualifying opportunity per property, so the lead list stays finite and useful.","Can a score go down?")
B.auo=new A.fX("The same intelligence type always keeps the same color and icon. Round markers are ranked opportunities. Diamond markers are supporting signals. Tap any marker or legend item for the source, timing, evidence, confidence, and next step.","What do the map colors and symbols mean?")
B.au_=new A.fX("The radar layer uses the official NOAA/NWS Multi-Radar Multi-Sensor reflectivity service. It is live weather context, not a meteorologist-verified hail swath or proof that a specific property was damaged.","Is the radar live?")
B.atM=new A.fX("The workspace refreshes on the interval selected in Settings. Each source also follows its own lawful source schedule. The live strip shows the next app sync; source cards show their health and refresh behavior.","How often does BridgePoint update?")
B.aur=new A.fX("Open an opportunity, choose Save opportunity, add a preset or custom note, and set the lead stage or next action. My Work keeps saved properties, follow-ups, claim tasks, and calendar work together.","How do I save an opportunity and follow up?")
B.atS=new A.fX("BridgePoint Company includes five seats, All Intelligence models, shared opportunities, shared notes and field visits, and owner/manager/member/viewer roles. Claims remain private unless a customer explicitly authorizes sharing.","How does the Company plan work?")
B.atJ=new A.fX("Field tracking is never hidden. A Company-plan user must explicitly start a field shift, sees a permanent sharing indicator, and can stop at any time. Owners, co-owners, and managers can see active teammates. Locations disappear from the live view after 15 minutes and are deleted after seven days.","How does Live Field Assist protect privacy?")
B.atN=new A.fX("A co-owner is a separate verified backup account for a trusted person. They can manage the company workspace and help when the primary owner is unavailable. Only the primary owner can appoint a co-owner or change the primary owner.","What is a co-owner?")
B.aum=new A.fX("Yes. Open Settings and choose Change plan / manage billing. Stripe securely handles plan changes, monthly or annual billing, payment methods, invoices, and cancellation.","Can I change my plan later?")
B.atG=new A.fX("Eligible new customers can explore the included package for seven days. A payment method is not required to begin the trial. The first ten paying customers also receive 50% off their selected plan for the first six monthly payments when eligible.","How does the 7-day free trial work?")
B.atV=new A.fX("Use the bell or Settings to choose Daily Brief, critical opportunity, saved follow-up, source-health, in-app, and device-push preferences. Device push also requires browser or operating-system permission.","How do notifications work?")
B.atZ=new A.fX("It is a chronological property story combining source evidence, signals, transitions, saved work, notes, and authorized claim events so users can understand what changed and when.","What is the property timeline?")
B.atO=new A.fX("BridgePoint shows planned markets so customers can request them. A state cannot be sold or unlocked until its property inventory, automatic source pipelines, scoring, legal access, and quality checks are live.","Why are other states visible but locked?")
B.aue=new A.fX("BridgePoint Homeowner is a lower-cost workspace for monitoring one home with plain-language property context, live weather, a property timeline, maintenance or claim reminders, notes, and alerts.","What is the Homeowner plan?")
B.atF=new A.fX("Yes. The hosted web app is installable from Chrome, Edge, and supported mobile browsers using Install app or Add to Home Screen. Native store releases require the normal Apple and Google signing and review steps.","Can I install BridgePoint on my device?")
B.auq=new A.fX("Open the source and timeline details first to check the source date. Then use Settings \u2192 Suggestions & feedback and choose Data request or Something is not working. Include the property and the field that needs review.","What should I do if information looks old or wrong?")
B.atL=new A.fX("Customer work is available only through authenticated, checked APIs. Direct access to private workspace tables is denied. Team roles control company access, and sensitive claim details remain private by default.","How does BridgePoint protect customer data?")
